@startuml log-reviewer
title LogReviewer — one scan of one target\nEnds when the findings exist; it does not wait for the fixes

scale 0.9
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam ArrowColor Black
skinparam StateBorderColor Black
skinparam StateFontColor Black
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor White
skinparam NoteBorderColor Black
skinparam state {
    BackgroundColor LightYellow
    BackgroundColor<<Package>> LightBlue
    BackgroundColor<<Final>> LightGreen
    BackgroundColor<<Error>> LightCoral
}

state "lr_pending" as Pending
    Pending: - tick received, no run dispatched
    Pending: - target: repo, service, environment

state "lr_working" as Working
    Working: - LogReviewer running
    Working: - queries Grafana / Loki

state "lr_done" as Done <<Final>>
    Done: - produced N findings, or none
    Done: - each NEW fingerprint opens a FixImplementer

state "lr_failed" as Failed <<Error>>
    Failed: - the scan failed
    Failed: - nothing to remember, it runs again next tick

[*] -d-> Pending: OnScheduledScan

Pending -d-> Working: handleStateLrPending\nOnPeriodicCheck(dispatch owed)\nOnSystemRecovery(dispatch owed)
Working -d-> Done: OnSandboxRunSucceeded\nOnPeriodicCheck(run finished)\nOnSystemRecovery(run finished)
Working -d[#Red]-> Failed: OnSandboxRunFailed\nOnPeriodicCheck(run died)\nOnSystemRecovery(run died)

Done -d-> [*]
Failed -d-> [*]

note left of Done
  The fan-out (1 scan -> N findings) is why this cannot be
  one machine with FixImplementer: a single instance cannot
  be in five states at once. Compare with Linear, which is
  1:1:1 and therefore holds two agents in one machine.

  A scan "still open because 2 of 5 fixes are running"
  enables no decision. The grouped report is a query by
  originating scan.
end note

note right of Failed
  This machine exists for homogeneity, not for information:
  its states mirror the run status. Since every SandboxRun
  hangs off a request (cron included), the scan needed an
  owner anyway, so the uniform shape costs nothing.
end note
@enduml
